OL,3,GNEWSADemolition plans submitted for old
OL,4,AToys R Us site
OL,5,
OL,6,FPlans have been filed to demolish the
OL,7,Fformer Toys R Us building in
OL,8,FSouthampton as part of the next step
OL,9,Ftowards redeveloping the site.
OL,11,FWBS Growth Partnership, which owns the
OL,12,F4.6-acre site near the city's central
OL,13,Frailway station, has applied for prior
OL,14,Fapproval to demolish the building while
OL,15,Fkeeping its steel frame and internal
OL,16,Fstructure.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
